# TF notes

Have to do an iterative apply if going from scratch here...
`TF_CLI_ARGS` in the environment variables is your friend.

To get around the "invalid count":

-target module.tls_certs_newer_global

Then to create the KVs before they are looked up with data:
-target module.vault_prereqs -target module.vault_prereqs_dr

THEN the whole potato

For destroy:
* a partial destroy with error will need more targeting....

# Bastion notes
```
apt-get install unzip podman
curl -O https://releases.hashicorp.com/vault/1.21.1+ent/vault_1.21.1+ent_linux_amd64.zip
unzip vault_1.21.1+ent_linux_amd64.zip vault
sudo mv vault /usr/local/bin
```
